cat > src/skills/alpha/SKILL.md <<EOF
---
name: alpha
description: Does the first thing.
---
# Alpha
EOF
cat > src/skills/alpha/references/notes.md <<EOF
Notes
EOF
cat > src/skills/beta/SKILL.md <<EOF
---
name: beta
description: Does the second thing.
---
# Beta
EOF
mkdir -p app
cd app
detoo skills
Installs the agent skills that drive adr, rfc, ust, plm, sop and fyr, keeps
them up to date, and removes them.  The skills come from detoo's repository
on GitHub, mustardcustarddev/detoo, unless you name another source.

detoo installs skills where the skills CLI (`npx skills`) does, and records
them in the same lock files, so either tool can update or remove what the
other installed:

* each skill is installed once, in `.agents/skills`, which Codex, Cursor,
  Gemini CLI, GitHub Copilot, OpenCode, Amp and Cline read;
* the directory of each agent that looks elsewhere, such as Claude Code's
  `.claude/skills`, gets a link to it;
* `skills-lock.json`, in the project's directory, records where each skill
  came from, so that `detoo skills update` can update it.  Commit it with the
  skills.

The project is the nearest of the current directory and its parents that
holds `skills-lock.json`, `.agents` or `.git`, below your home directory.  If
none does, it is the current directory.

With `--global`, skills are installed for your user, in every project:
in `~/.agents/skills`, linked into each agent's own directory, such as
`~/.claude/skills`, and recorded in `~/.agents/.skill-lock.json`.

Each command says what it is doing as it goes, on stderr.

Usage:
  detoo skills [flags]
  detoo skills [command]

Examples:
  # Install every skill in this project, for Claude Code and the agents found:
  detoo skills install

  # Bring the installed skills up to date:
  detoo skills update

  # Remove a skill:
  detoo skills remove create-adr

Available Commands:
  install     Install agent skills, by default every skill detoo offers
  remove      Remove installed agent skills
  update      Update installed agent skills from their sources, by default every one

Flags:
  -h, --help   help for skills

Use "detoo skills [command] --help" for more information about a command.
echo $?
1
detoo skills install --source ~/src alpha gamma
Reading skills from ~/src…
Found 2 skills.
detoo: unknown skill gamma: ~/src offers alpha, beta
echo $?
1
detoo skills install --source ~/src --agent vim
detoo: unknown agent "vim": choose from claude-code, codex, cursor, gemini-cli, github-copilot, opencode, amp, cline, windsurf, roo, kiro-cli, goose, continue, junie, qwen-code, augment, trae
echo $?
1
detoo skills install --source nowhere
detoo: "nowhere" is not a source: give a repository on GitHub, such as mustardcustarddev/detoo, or a directory, such as ./skills
echo $?
1
detoo skills install --source ./missing
Reading skills from ./missing…
detoo: cannot read skills from ./missing: there is no such directory
echo $?
1
detoo skills install --source ~/src --list alpha
detoo: give --list alone, or with --source
echo $?
1
detoo skills update
No skills are recorded in skills-lock.json. Install them with detoo skills install.
echo $?
0
detoo skills update alpha
detoo: unknown skill alpha: skills-lock.json does not record it
echo $?
1
detoo skills remove
detoo: name the skills to remove, or give --all
echo $?
1
detoo skills remove --all alpha
detoo: give --all, or name the skills to remove, not both
echo $?
1
detoo skills remove alpha
detoo: unknown skill alpha: it is not installed in .agents/skills
echo $?
1
